Abstract N°: 5493
Real-world experience with lebrikizumab in moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis: a case series of eight
patients from Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet"
Beatriz Clemente Hernández
1
, Alba Navarro Bielsa
1
, Itziar Muelas Rives
1
, Iranzu Barandika Urrutia
1
, Zita Alvarez
Bobillo
1
, Jorge Arostegui Aguilar
1
, Ignacio Hernandez Aragues
1
, Tamara Gracia-Cazaña
1
, Yolanda Gilaberte
1
1
Miguel Servet University Hospital, Dermatology, Zaragoza, Spain
Introduction & Objectives:
Lebrikizumab, a monoclonal antibody targeting IL-13, has shown efficacy in clinical trials for the treatment of
moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis. We present a series of 8 patients treated with Lebrikizumab in real-life
clinical practice at our hospital, aiming to describe their clinical profiles, treatment efficacy, and safety outcomes.
Materials & Methods:
Clinical data were retrospectively collected from 8 patients with moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis who
initiated treatment with Lebrikizumab between [November/2024] and [March/2025] at the Hospital Universitario
Miguel Servet. Data included demographics, comorbidities, prior treatments, clinical response 
(
EASI, DLQI, NRS
pruritus
)
, and adverse events, assessed during follow-up.
Results:
A total of 8 patients 
(
3 women, 5 men; mean age 42.0 years
)
 were included. Atopic comorbidities were present in
4 patients 
(
44%
)
. All patients had previously received topical treatments. Regarding systemic therapies, prior
treatments included ciclosporin 
(
5, 55.6%
)
, dupilumab 
(
5, 55.6%
)
, tralokinumab 
(
3, 33.3%
)
, abrocitinib 
(
2, 22.2%
)
,
and upadacitinib 
(
2, 22.2%
)
. Clinical outcomes at week 16 are under analysis. No serious adverse events or
treatment discontinuations were reported at the time of writing.
Conclusion:
Lebrikizumab appears to be an effective and well-tolerated treatment option in our real-world cohort of patients
with moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis. These preliminary results are consistent with those observed in clinical
trials.
