)
a Integrated analysis of ADvocate1, ADvocate2, KGAF and ADhere 
(
Weeks 0-16
)
; b Lebrikizumab 500 mg at Week
0 and Week 2, followed by 250 mg Q2W; cIncludes preferred terms of conjunctivitis and conjunctivitis bacterial.
Conclusions:
 LEB safety reported in the SmPC is consistent with the large body of evidence on LEB safety. LEB has
a positive benefit-risk in adults and adolescent patients with moderate to severe AD, with most AE being mild or
moderate in severity and few leading to treatment discontinuation. The incidence of conjunctivitis did not increase
with longer exposure to LEB.
