children, with intense itch and discomfort affecting daily activities, emotional well-being, and social interactions.
Population variations in AD presentation and severity warrant further analysis of dupilumab treatment effects on
patient-reported outcomes across racial subgroups. This study assessed long-term changes in patient-reported
QoL, sleep loss, and itch intensity, as well as safety and discontinuation rates across self-identified racial subgroups
in pediatric patients treated with dupilumab for 
≤
3 yr.
