Introduction & Objectives:
 Atopic dermatitis 
(
AD
)
 significantly impairs quality of life 
(
QoL
)
, with pruritus and
sleep disturbance being major burdens. While dupilumab has proven efficacy in reducing skin symptoms, its direct
impact on sleep and QoL deserves further investigation. This systematic review and meta-analysis aims to assess
the effect of dupilumab on QoL and sleep in adults with AD.
Materials & Methods:
 A systematic search was conducted in PubMed, Embase, and Cochrane, following PRISMA
guidelines. Only randomized controlled trials were included. Statistical analyses were performed using Review
Manager. A random-effects model was performed to determine the proportion with a 95% confidence interval
(
CI
)
. Heterogeneity was evaluated through I2 statistics.
Results:
 A total of 9 studies were included, comprising 3,351 patients, of whom 2,129 
(
63.5%
)
 received dupilumab.
The mean age of participants was 35.6 years, with a mean proportion of male patients of 58.2%. At baseline, the
average Dermatology Life Quality Index 
(
DLQI
)
 score was 15.2.
There was a significant reduction in DLQI scores in the dupilumab group compared to placebo 
(
