JADE EXTEND if they received placebo in the qualifying phase 3 trials. Assessments included the proportion of
patients in the long-term efficacy pool who maintained response for EASI-75/-90, 
≥
4-point improvement from
baseline in Peak Pruritus Numerical Rating Scale 
(
PP-NRS4; used with permission from Regeneron
Pharmaceuticals, Inc., and Sanofi
)
, PP-NRS score of 0 or 1 
(
PP-NRS 0/1
)
, 
≥
4-point improvement from baseline in
Dermatology Life Quality Index 
(
DLQI-4
)
 and 
≥
6-point improvement from baseline in Children
’
s Dermatology Life
Quality Index 
(
CDLQI-6
)
 to 116 weeks at 100% of visits and at 80% of visits, respectively. Missing data were
handled with nonresponder imputation.
Results:
 At Week 16 of abrocitinib treatment, response criteria were met by 663 and 361 patients in the
abrocitinib 200-mg and 100-mg arms, respectively. Substantial proportions of patients treated with abrocitinib at
either dose maintained response at 80% of visits to Week 116 for EASI-75 
(
200 mg: 62.3%, 100 mg: 52.6%
)
, PP-
NRS4 
(
47.1%, 35.5%
)
, the high-threshold responses EASI-90 
(
