Abstract N°: 7991
Tolerance and efficacy of a new emollient 
“
Plus
”
 containing Aquaphilus Dolomiae and Dextran sodium
sulfate extracts in improving long-term atopic skin condition
Marine Rodeghiero
1
, Camille BOUDET
2
, Gautier Doat
2
, Marie-Dominique Thouvenin*
1
1
Pierre Fabre Dermo-Cosmetics & Personal Care, R&D Department, Toulouse, France
2
Pierre Fabre Dermo-Cosmetics & Personal Care, Laboratoire Dermatologique Eau Thermale Avène, Lavaur, France
Introduction & Objectives:
 Emollients are considered as the first-line therapy of atopic dermatitis 
(
AD
)
management. Their prolonged application has been shown to improve skin condition, patient
’
s quality of life and
space-out flare-ups. These products must be safe, effective and suitable for infants, children and adults. This study
aimed to assess the tolerance and efficacy of a new emollient 
“
Plus
”
 containing 
Aquaphilus Dolomiae
 and 
Dextran
sodium sulfate
 extracts, intended to improve long-term atopic skin condition.
Materials & Methods:
 66 Subjects from 5 months to 56 years old were included in a 3-month-long open clinical
study. Main inclusion criteria were mild AD with SCORAD between 10 and 25, xerosis intensity 
≥
 2 
(
scale 0-3
)
 and
pruritus intensity 
≥
 3 
(
scale 0-10
)
, and at least one peak of xerosis and pruritus per month reported by the
subjects/parents during the 3 previous months. Assessments included tolerance, AD severity 
(
SCORAD index
)
,
quality of life 
(
Dermatology Life Quality Index for adults, children and infants; DLQI, CDLQI, IDLQI
)
, number of
peaks of xerosis and pruritus, tolerance, and cosmetic acceptability. **
Results:
 After 3 months of twice-daily use, tolerance was assessed as very good by the investigators
(
dermatologist and pediatrician
)
. AD severity significantly improved with a SCORAD index decrease by 
–
77%
(
p<0.0001
)
. Xerosis and pruritus respectively decreased by 79% and 85% 
(
p<0.0001
)
 and a significant
improvement in quality of life was observed 
(
DLQI: + 66%, CDLQI +91%, IDLQI +57%, 
(
p<0.0001
))
. Moreover, 97%
of the subjects did not report any peak of xerosis and itching during the study. Finally, the cosmetic acceptability
of the product was evaluated as very good with subjects declaring their skin comfortable and soothed.**
Conclusion:
 The efficacy results of this study demonstrate the benefits of this new emollient 
“
Plus
”
 in improving
the long-term management of atopic skin conditions. Moreover, its very good tolerance and acceptability by the
patients could help to ensure long-term compliance.
